### bc_stack_ref_inv_MutBlock_centre
  (* the invariant of the longer stack holds of the same f and tf:
     the pointer of the reference is what v_inv gives (its Thunk
     cases are out because the reference is a MutBlock), the block
     is what bc_ref_inv gives for the reference, which is reachable
     from the stack, and the centre of the payload is the value at
     the index that the goal reads.  The three parts of the
     invariant that the longer stack changes are all_ts (which only
     grows), all_vs (where the centre is a value of the refs
     already) and the reachability (where the centre reaches no
     more than the pointer does) *)
